    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`RotaryEmbedding.forward_xpu` sends every full-rotary head size that has no fused path to `sgl_kernel.rotary_embedding`. That kernel only accepts head sizes 32, 64, 96, 128 and 256 and raises a `RuntimeError` on anything else.\n\nThe EAGLE3 draft for Qwen3-32B (`AngelSlim/Qwen3-32B_eagle3`) has head_dim 80. Serving Qwen3-32B with that draft on XPU therefore crashes the server on the first draft forward.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `layers/rotary_embedding/base.py`:\n  - New `_XPU_ROTARY_EMBEDDING_HEAD_SIZES`, the head sizes `sgl_kernel.rotary_embedding` accepts.\n  - `forward_xpu` sends any other full-rotary head size to `forward_native`, as it already does for partial rotary.\n- Supported head sizes still take the kernel, so existing models are unaffected.\n- New `test/registered/xpu/test_rope_xpu.py`: it checks head size 80 (neox and non-neox) against `forward_native`. Without this fix it fails with the kernel's `RuntimeError`; with it, it passes.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- `test_rope_xpu.py` passes on Arc Pro B70 with sgl-kernel-xpu 0.4.0 and 0.5.0. The head sizes the kernel supports did not change between those versions.\n- No behavior change for supported head sizes.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot a performance change: supported head sizes keep the kernel path. Only unsupported head sizes, which used to crash, take the native path. For the Qwen3-32B EAGLE3 draft that is a single layer.\n\nThe draft's attention needs a separate fix (#46998). With both, Qwen3-32B + EAGLE3 on 4x B70 reaches 42.4 tok/s at c=1, against 31.5 tok/s without speculative decoding. That run used greedy ShareGPT prompts and 3 draft steps with topk 1.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41861258477](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41861258477)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41861257754](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41861257754)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41861258212](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41861258212)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
